Subject: Cantor Field Attention Fault Assurance P0 Justification

@ [justification_uuid] 7e186597-97d5-466b-82fb-bb3ddbf31d1d
@ [source_manifest] C:\Project\Cantor\source_documents\2026-08-18_field_attention_fault_assurance\Source_Document_Manifest.sop
@ [exploded] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\exploded\Cantor_Field_Attention_Fault_Assurance_P0.exploded.sop

& [Problem] is one valid boolean conceals whether an external failure is reproducible from retained bytes

& [Decision] is an additive closed assurance enum on ReportVerification
  + the enum makes evidence strength machine-visible without rewriting historical CycleReport bytes
  + response-backed faults retain exact reconstruction requirements
  + structural runtime faults remain valid as canonical declarations but carry no response-backed implication
  + deterministic and provider-backed positive paths remain distinguishable

& [Alternatives] are rejected
  - rejecting every response-less runtime fault is rejected because it erases bounded operational evidence
  - treating every canonical fault path as response-backed is rejected because shape does not prove external cause
  - free-text assurance is rejected because callers require finite stable handling

& [Nonclaim] is that assurance class does not prove truth safety causation provider honesty or external-world correspondence
